  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "A dodgy video is the same problem as a dodgy avatar; VRC solves this problem via allowing users to put junior accounts in baby jail and auto-hide their avatars, or even automatically mute them.\n\nUntrusted URL blocking in publics should be a trust rank feature; if an account is too junior, URLs they submit are prevented from being used by receiving clients with the trust rank setting set to filter out untrusted URLs.\n\nSome notes on the above:\n\n1. This empowers users more than the initial blanket ban\n\n2. This doesn't require undoing any current work VRC has done on this\n\n3. This makes this trust-and-safety feature be consistent with other user content, and users love consistency\n\n4. Users who are unhappy and can tolerate the occasional UristMcShitter 45fb posting a gore video can just disable the feature and keep on keeping on",
